# Boot logs from the first real hardware bring-up (see KNOWN_ISSUES.md's
# Round 13) detected a 32MB flash chip on the ESP32-P4-Pico, while the
# default config assumes 2MB -- ESP-IDF then limits itself to the smaller
# configured size and logs a mismatch warning on every boot. This doesn't
# risk corruption (the current image fits well within 2MB either way), but
# leaves the rest of the chip's flash unusable for OTA or larger assets
# until the configured size matches reality.
#
# This intentionally only fixes the flash-size mismatch, not the partition
# table -- the partition layout stays at its current (small) size since
# nothing here needs the extra space yet; grow the partition table
# separately (see c6-firmware/sdkconfig.defaults for that pattern) if a
# future feature actually needs more than the current app partition offers.
#
# If your specific P4-Pico board has different flash, override this with
# `idf.py menuconfig` -> "Serial flasher config" -> "Flash size", or lower
# the value below to match.
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_32MB=y
